BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mealplan-20260907-breakfast-1@mealplanner
DTSTAMP:20260906T135947Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260907T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260907T090000
SUMMARY:🍳 Breakfast: Breakfast Burrito
DESCRIPTION:Recipe: Breakfast Burrito\nServings: 2\nPrep: 5 min | Cook: 10 min | Total: 15 min\n\n--- Ingredients ---\n• 4 eggs\n• 2 large flour tortillas\n• 4 slice bacon\n• 0.5 cup shredded cheddar cheese\n• 0.25 cup salsa\n• 1 tbsp butter\n• 1 avocado\n\n--- Steps ---\n1. Cook bacon in a skillet until crispy. Remove and chop.\n2. Whisk eggs, melt butter in the same skillet, and scramble eggs over medium heat.\n3. Warm tortillas in microwave for 15 seconds.\n4. Fill each tortilla with eggs, bacon, cheese, sliced avocado, and salsa.\n5. Fold and roll into burritos. Optional: toast seam-side down in a dry pan for 1 minute.\n\nTip: Meal prep: wrap in foil and freeze. Reheat in microwave 2-3 min.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mealplan-20260907-lunch-2@mealplanner
DTSTAMP:20260906T135947Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260907T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260907T130000
SUMMARY:🥗 Lunch: Breakfast Burrito (leftover)
DESCRIPTION:Recipe: Breakfast Burrito\n(Leftover - no cooking needed!)\nServings: 2\nPrep: 5 min | Cook: 10 min | Total: 15 min\n\nTip: Meal prep: wrap in foil and freeze. Reheat in microwave 2-3 min.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mealplan-20260907-dinner-3@mealplanner
DTSTAMP:20260906T135947Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260907T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260907T193000
SUMMARY:🍽️ Dinner: Garlic Butter Pasta
DESCRIPTION:Recipe: Garlic Butter Pasta\nServings: 4\nPrep: 5 min | Cook: 15 min | Total: 20 min\n\n--- Ingredients ---\n• 1 lb spaghetti\n• 4 tbsp butter\n• 6 clove garlic\n• 0.5 tsp red pepper flakes\n• 0.5 cup parmesan cheese\n• 0.25 cup fresh parsley\n• 1 tbsp olive oil\n• 1 lemon\n\n--- Steps ---\n1. Cook spaghetti in salted water according to package. Reserve 1 cup pasta water before draining.\n2. Mince garlic. Melt butter with olive oil in a large pan over medium heat.\n3. Add garlic and red pepper flakes, cook 1-2 minutes until fragrant (don't burn).\n4. Add drained pasta and 1/2 cup reserved pasta water. Toss to coat.\n5. Add parmesan, squeeze of lemon juice, and parsley. Toss again, adding more pasta water if needed.\n\nTip: Add grilled chicken or shrimp for protein. Works with any pasta shape.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mealplan-20260908-breakfast-4@mealplanner
DTSTAMP:20260906T135947Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260908T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260908T090000
SUMMARY:🍳 Breakfast: Overnight Oats
DESCRIPTION:Recipe: Overnight Oats\nServings: 2\nPrep: 5 min | Total: 5 min\n\n--- Ingredients ---\n• 1 cup rolled oats\n• 1 cup milk\n• 0.5 cup greek yogurt\n• 2 tbsp honey\n• 0.5 cup blueberries\n• 2 tbsp chia seeds\n\n--- Steps ---\n1. Combine oats, milk, yogurt, honey, and chia seeds in a jar or container.\n2. Stir well, cover, and refrigerate overnight (or at least 4 hours).\n3. Top with blueberries before serving. Eat cold or microwave 1-2 min.\n\nTip: Swap blueberries for banana, strawberries, or any fruit. Add peanut butter for extra protein.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
